+Recovery MUST determine modeled-World commitment authority only from the atomic World version + WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT + committed-event delivery-intent triple, never from outcome-event delivery alone. A missing triple proves that this candidate did not make an authoritative World commit; it DOES NOT prove that a tool call or external side effect did not occur. When the triple exists, World authority is already established and only post-commit delivery may resume idempotently; the original World mutation MUST NOT be replayed.
+
+Before any crash recovery retry or compensation, Veda MUST correlate the original stable action/operation identity, authorization reference, tool attempt, external idempotency key where applicable, observation and provider evidence. If an external effect was submitted but its result is UNKNOWN, Veda MUST reconcile the authoritative external state before deciding a new action. If reconciliation is inconclusive, it MUST durably record UNKNOWN and enter RECOVERY_REQUIRED or escalate; it MUST NOT blindly retry the external effect, invent a failed outcome or claim World success.
+
+RETRY_COMMIT_AFTER_REVALIDATION means a new attempt to commit the already-observed and freshly verified candidate modeled-World transition under a current authorized exact-parent CAS check. It is NOT permission to re-execute an external action. A fresh external action or compensation requires its own applicable authorization, stable identity/idempotency controls and independent external-effect verification. The runtime then determines whether to:
 
