+A RecoveryReceipt is durable evidence of a recovery attempt, its verification
+and residual risks. It is NOT a WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT, cannot prove an
+authoritative modeled-World version and MUST NOT independently authorize
+World mutation. If recovery changes canonical modeled World State, its
+RecoveryReceipt MUST reference the distinct genuine WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT
+produced by a separately authorized, freshly verified World Kernel exact-parent
+CAS commit. A compensation or corrective external action is a separate
+externally observable operation requiring its own authorization, stable
+identity/idempotency controls, evidence and reconciliation; it is not World
+rollback by rewriting history.
